    "html": "<h2>Major Forensic Breakthroughs</h2>\n\n<p>Through systematic local Whisper ASR dialogue extraction combined with Jerry Haendiges (<code>jjonez</code>) network logs, J. David Goldin's database, and contemporary broadcast logs, we have resolved <strong>50 previously undated or corrupted radio recordings</strong>.</p>\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>1. <em>Gunsmoke</em> Mysteries Resolved</h3>\n- <strong>\"Ambush at Medicine Lodge\" ➔ <em>\"The Gypsum Hills Feud\"</em> (April 16, 1955)</strong>: Circulated for decades under the spurious collector title <em>\"Ambush at Medicine Lodge\"</em>. Internal dialogue reveals Matt Dillon and Chester interceding in a blood feud between the Peavey and Cade families in the Gypsum Hills near Medicine Lodge, featuring an on-air CBS promo for the television series <em>Mr. Citizen</em> (aired spring 1955).\n- <strong>\"Andy Gilman\" ➔ <em>\"Bringing Down Father\"</em> (March 11, 1956)</strong>: Circulated in AFRS collections as undated <em>\"Andy Gilman\"</em>. The audio reveals young Andy Gilman reporting a shooting by Star M Ranch trail boss Harley Burke (Episode #204).\n- <strong>\"Bannocks Circus\" ➔ <em>\"Wagon Show\"</em> (May 24, 1959)</strong>: Circulated in AFRS as <em>\"Bannocks Circus\"</em>. Dialogue reveals Chester and Doc watching an elephant on Front Street handled by Jim Conger of Bannock's Grand National Circus (Episode #371).\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>2. <em>The Whistler</em> April 1948 Rebroadcast Run</h3>\nFour generic recordings labeled <em>\"The Part 10\"</em> through <em>\"The Part 13\"</em> were identified as consecutive weekly Wednesday broadcasts from April 1948 on CBS West Coast:\n- <strong>\"The Part 10\"</strong> ➔ <strong>\"Bird of Prey\"</strong> (March 31, 1948, Ep #304)\n- <strong>\"The Part 11\"</strong> ➔ <strong>\"What Makes a Murderer?\"</strong> (April 7, 1948, Ep #305, starring Frank Lovejoy and Joan Banks)\n- <strong>\"The Part 12\"</strong> ➔ <strong>\"Till Death Do Us Part\"</strong> (April 14, 1948, Ep #306, starring Doris Singleton & Gerald Mohr, preceded by a White House presidential address)\n- <strong>\"The Part 13\"</strong> ➔ <strong>\"The Silent City\"</strong> (April 21, 1948, Ep #307)\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>3. <em>Sherlock Holmes</em> Tri-Decade \"Blue Carbuncle\" Set</h3>\nThree undated recordings of <em>\"The Adventure of the Blue Carbuncle\"</em> were anchored to their specific historical productions:\n- <strong>1948-12-26</strong>: Mutual broadcast starring John Stanley and Alfred Shirley, sponsored by Clipper Craft Clothes.\n- <strong>1954-12-14</strong>: BBC Light Programme production starring Sir John Gielgud and Sir Ralph Richardson.\n- <strong>1977-07-25</strong>: <em>CBS Radio Mystery Theater</em> production starring Kevin McCarthy, hosted by E.G. Marshall.\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3>4. <em>Fibber McGee and Molly</em> Special Recoveries</h3>\n- <strong>\"Xx Xx\" (Untitled)</strong> ➔ <strong>\"Christmas Seal Show: Fibber McGee and Molly\"</strong> (1951-12-01): National Tuberculosis Association special hosted by Harlow Wilcox.\n- <strong>\"24 On The Night Before Christmas\"</strong> ➔ <strong>\"The Night Before Christmas\"</strong> (1946-12-24): Original Christmas Eve 1946 NBC broadcast sponsored by Johnson's Wax.\n- <strong>\"Bob Hope\"</strong> ➔ <strong>\"June Is Dairy Month: Salute with Fibber McGee and Bob Hope\"</strong> (1953-06-01): California Dairy Industry Advisory Board special written by Phil Leslie.",
    "markdown": "# Unlocking 50 \"Date Unknown\" Radio Classics: Forensic Transcripts Solve Longstanding OTR Mysteries\n\n**Date**: 2026-08-21  \n**Author**: RadioIndex Archival Team  \n**Tags**: Gunsmoke, The Whistler, Sherlock Holmes, Fibber McGee, Escape, Archival Discovery\n\n---\n\n## Major Forensic Breakthroughs\n\nThrough systematic local Whisper ASR dialogue extraction combined with Jerry Haendiges (`jjonez`) network logs, J. David Goldin's database, and contemporary broadcast logs, we have resolved **50 previously undated or corrupted radio recordings**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. *Gunsmoke* Mysteries Resolved\n- **\"Ambush at Medicine Lodge\" ➔ *\"The Gypsum Hills Feud\"* (April 16, 1955)**: Circulated for decades under the spurious collector title *\"Ambush at Medicine Lodge\"*. Internal dialogue reveals Matt Dillon and Chester interceding in a blood feud between the Peavey and Cade families in the Gypsum Hills near Medicine Lodge, featuring an on-air CBS promo for the television series *Mr. Citizen* (aired spring 1955).\n- **\"Andy Gilman\" ➔ *\"Bringing Down Father\"* (March 11, 1956)**: Circulated in AFRS collections as undated *\"Andy Gilman\"*. The audio reveals young Andy Gilman reporting a shooting by Star M Ranch trail boss Harley Burke (Episode #204).\n- **\"Bannocks Circus\" ➔ *\"Wagon Show\"* (May 24, 1959)**: Circulated in AFRS as *\"Bannocks Circus\"*. Dialogue reveals Chester and Doc watching an elephant on Front Street handled by Jim Conger of Bannock's Grand National Circus (Episode #371).\n\n---\n\n### 2. *The Whistler* April 1948 Rebroadcast Run\nFour generic recordings labeled *\"The Part 10\"* through *\"The Part 13\"* were identified as consecutive weekly Wednesday broadcasts from April 1948 on CBS West Coast:\n- **\"The Part 10\"** ➔ **\"Bird of Prey\"** (March 31, 1948, Ep #304)\n- **\"The Part 11\"** ➔ **\"What Makes a Murderer?\"** (April 7, 1948, Ep #305, starring Frank Lovejoy and Joan Banks)\n- **\"The Part 12\"** ➔ **\"Till Death Do Us Part\"** (April 14, 1948, Ep #306, starring Doris Singleton & Gerald Mohr, preceded by a White House presidential address)\n- **\"The Part 13\"** ➔ **\"The Silent City\"** (April 21, 1948, Ep #307)\n\n---\n\n### 3. *Sherlock Holmes* Tri-Decade \"Blue Carbuncle\" Set\nThree undated recordings of *\"The Adventure of the Blue Carbuncle\"* were anchored to their specific historical productions:\n- **1948-12-26**: Mutual broadcast starring John Stanley and Alfred Shirley, sponsored by Clipper Craft Clothes.\n- **1954-12-14**: BBC Light Programme production starring Sir John Gielgud and Sir Ralph Richardson.\n- **1977-07-25**: *CBS Radio Mystery Theater* production starring Kevin McCarthy, hosted by E.G. Marshall.\n\n---\n\n### 4. *Fibber McGee and Molly* Special Recoveries\n- **\"Xx Xx\" (Untitled)** ➔ **\"Christmas Seal Show: Fibber McGee and Molly\"** (1951-12-01): National Tuberculosis Association special hosted by Harlow Wilcox.\n- **\"24 On The Night Before Christmas\"** ➔ **\"The Night Before Christmas\"** (1946-12-24): Original Christmas Eve 1946 NBC broadcast sponsored by Johnson's Wax.\n- **\"Bob Hope\"** ➔ **\"June Is Dairy Month: Salute with Fibber McGee and Bob Hope\"** (1953-06-01): California Dairy Industry Advisory Board special written by Phil Leslie.\n"
